1
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:20,200
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATION)

2
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:24,720
-Excuse me, where's the director?
-What?

3
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,160
Where is the director?

4
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:27,680
Go fuck yourself!

5
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:30,480
(THEME SONG PLAYING)

6
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:36,200
ALESSANDRO
the intern

7
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:38,600
CORINNA
the star

8
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:40,040
ARIANNA
the assistant director

9
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:46,200
ITALA
the script supervisor

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,760
GLORIA
the makeup artist

11
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:54,320
STANIS
the celebrity

12
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:59,880
RENÉ
the director

13
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:02,200
LOPEZ
the network executive

14
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:08,720
DUCCIO
the director of photography

15
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:10,400
BIASCICA
the master electrician

16
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:15,280
SERGIO
the production manager

17
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:16,960
LORENZO
the slave

18
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:32,560
BIASCICA: Plug it in, come on!
MAN 2: It's too far.

19
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:35,600
It's easy. Come on!
Stretch out those arms!

20
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:36,760
I can't reach.

21
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:40,680
Damn you, always wasting my time.

22
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:43,480
I'll hang you on to that cable. Come on!

23
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:50,000
(EXHALES)

24
00:01:56,040 --> 00:01:59,600
Yes, of course.
But, listen to me, Boris.

25
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:02,200
This must be a great direction.

26
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:05,080
I want you focused.
Just like last year. Okay?

27
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:08,440
We have to kill it, Boris!

28
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:10,840
-Come on!
-Sorry, but are you the director?

29
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:13,080
Lopez is here.

30
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:15,360
(SIGHS)

31
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:16,720
Who are you? What is it?

32
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:19,360
Well, I'm the intern, uh...

33
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:21,080
-I just wanted...
-No, you don't.

34
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:24,360
Stay here, be quiet,
and wait to be told what to do. Okay?

35
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:26,120
(SCREAMS) Yes.

36
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:28,880
MAN: Are you flying now?
Beetle.

37
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:31,280
What are you doing?

38
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:32,560
It's not your department.

39
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:33,680
Uh...

40
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:34,880
(SMACKS LIPS)

41
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:40,400
STUDIO 2

42
00:02:57,280 --> 00:02:58,840
THE EYES OF THE HEART

43
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:02,920
Everyone says doing a second season
of The Eyes of the Heart is foolish.

44
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:07,400
They say, "They cancelled it after
three episodes and you're doing another?"

45
00:03:07,480 --> 00:03:10,080
Are you an idiot? Are you stupid?

46
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:11,200
(LAUGHS)

47
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:15,280
So Dr. Cane is stupid
for believing in this project?

48
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:19,200
So the Greeks are stupid
for purchasing the rights?

49
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:22,200
(SHEEP BLEATING)

50
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:31,280
They say "The Eyes of the Heart
was a flop."

51
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:33,920
No. It wasn't.

52
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,400
It was wrongly scheduled.

53
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:40,240
The time slot was wrong.

54
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:42,240
The time of year was wrong.

55
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:45,800
So getting cancelled was a defeat?

56
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:47,480
No, quite the opposite!

57
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:51,480
It prepared us for success.

58
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:56,840
Yes. Because now we can rebroadcast
the first season.

59
00:03:56,920 --> 00:04:02,200
But with a great, fantastic launch.
But...

60
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,600
We need a different mindset.
Yes, absolutely.

61
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:11,560
And I wonder, "Are you capable
of changing your mindset?"

62
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:13,320
Because, I'll warn you,

63
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:15,560
if you don't change your mindset,

64
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:19,120
we'll film this,
the final episode.

65
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:23,000
"The Attack,"
where all characters die and it all ends.

66
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:26,320
And you can all go home
to update your CVs.

67
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:29,680
Do you understand, René?

68
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:36,240
I know that I can trust you all.

69
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:39,560
Our great director of cinematography
is in top form.

70
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:42,120
Duccio is like new.

71
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:48,000
(CHUCKLE) And René Ferretti.
René is not a director.

72
00:04:48,320 --> 00:04:50,800
René is directing itself!

73
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:53,360
-(CHUCKLES)
-(PHONE BEEPING)

74
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:55,440
(CHUCKLES)

75
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:58,720
Dr. Cane sends his best wishes,
right on time.

76
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:00,760
What great timing!

77
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:03,120
INSUFFICIENT CREDIT

78
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:05,320
I add my wishes to his.

79
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:07,760
But remember,
you must change your mindset.

80
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:12,360
I want you to put your hearts
into The Eyes of the Heart 2.

81
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:13,960
Good luck, everyone!

82
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:15,440
Sir?

83
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:18,280
-Biascica, please.
-No, with all due respect.

84
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:21,080
Sir, we'll put our hearts into it.

85
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:23,760
And also our eyes. Both of them.

86
00:05:24,920 --> 00:05:28,120
But we're still waiting to be paid
for that overtime in April.

87
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:31,040
-What overtime, Biascica?
-Those for Libeccio.

88
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:33,760
You're still on that?
That was a year and a half ago!

89
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:36,120
Exactly. We've been waiting
a year and a half.

90
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:39,240
You guys won't ever see
that money, Biascica.

91
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:42,400
-But that's not right.
-Never!

92
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:45,280
That's messed up.
It's unfair.

93
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:47,000
-I know, Biascica.
-Go to hell!

94
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:48,920
-I'm sorry, but...
-Go to hell!

95
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,720
I even gave you a slave.
Should I take him back?

96
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:53,640
-No, don't.
-Yes, I will.

97
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:55,720
-No, don't take the slave.
-I will, okay?

98
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:57,560
Go to hell!

99
00:05:57,640 --> 00:06:00,800
Go to hell! Move!

100
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:01,960
Come on!

101
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:04,800
It's always the same
around here.

102
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:14,520
(GRUNTS)

103
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:21,800
We'll start from 168.
No smoking on set, thanks.

104
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:23,680
I saw you, Duccio. Put that out.

105
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:27,640
So, first: never speak
unless spoken to.

106
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:30,360
Second: if I ask you to do something,
just do it.

107
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:31,960
Third: you're not an intern.

108
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:35,800
You're a machine. Quick, like a ferret.
If you don't like it, you can leave.

109
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:38,120
Uh, that's fine. I'm Alessandro.

110
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:40,920
Yeah, whatever. Come with me.

111
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,960
-Biascica, could you use him?
-Yup!

112
00:06:43,040 --> 00:06:44,720
Go to Biascica. Come on.

113
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:47,360
What's your team?

114
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:49,200
I'm sorry?

115
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:52,280
What's your team?

116
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:56,640
My team is...

117
00:06:58,200 --> 00:07:00,240
My team is...

118
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:02,000
Roma?

119
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:05,320
(GRUNTS)

120
00:07:05,400 --> 00:07:06,800
Good.

121
00:07:06,880 --> 00:07:08,120
Do you see those stands?

122
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:09,680
-Where should I take them?
-No!

123
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:12,960
You must watch them.
They steal everything here.

124
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:15,160
And then make six coffees for the guys.

125
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:17,120
Seven, since you're a Roma fan.

126
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:18,320
Go Roma!

127
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:19,480
RENÉ: Okay, people.

128
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:23,280
Besides the bullshit Lopez said,
let's get serious. All right?

129
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:26,360
Starting with 168.
Duccio? Where's Duccio?

130
00:07:26,520 --> 00:07:28,960
Hey! You have half an hour,
this isn't Kubrick.

131
00:07:29,040 --> 00:07:30,080
Really?

132
00:07:31,880 --> 00:07:33,160
-Alfredo?
-Yes!

133
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:35,600
Be an assistant director.
I've yet to hear you!

134
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:39,680
Please, everyone. Silence!
Everyone ready with the 168, in 30!

135
00:07:39,760 --> 00:07:43,160
You heard the director,
be as quiet as mice!

136
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:45,280
-Was that okay?
-I like it.

137
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:48,280
Let's go.

138
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:51,840
(SCOFFS)

139
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:54,040
(SIGHS)

140
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:07,360
You're Lorenzo, right?
The cinematography intern.

141
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:13,600
Have you settled in a bit?

142
00:08:13,680 --> 00:08:15,560
Are you learning anything, huh?

143
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:20,640
Are you mute?

144
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:23,360
(WHISPERS)
They told me not to speak.

145
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:26,560
Shut up! You have to shut up!

146
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,400
STANIS: That lovely stage smell!

147
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:31,960
I feel at home.

148
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:34,400
And I envy you people, yes.

149
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:38,600
You artisans,
who get to work with your hands and eyes.

150
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:39,800
With wisdom.

151
00:08:40,440 --> 00:08:43,240
And it's out of the respect that I have
for the realness

152
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:45,040
that bleeds through these walls,

153
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:47,720
that I wish to express
a humble thought of mine.

154
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:49,640
Thank you, dear.

155
00:08:52,120 --> 00:08:54,160
You can all go fuck yourselves.

156
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:56,480
I'll quit this show
as soon as I get the chance.

157
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:58,360
I'm kidding. I feel great!

158
00:08:58,440 --> 00:09:01,040
-Look everyone, here he is!
-Yes!

159
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:04,080
Stanis La Rochelle. Legend. Genius!

160
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:05,320
I don't know this man.

161
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:07,720
-Hey!
-Hey! There he is. He never changes!

162
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,480
-Hey, Stanis, how are you?
-I'm good, thank you.

163
00:09:10,560 --> 00:09:12,360
-Did you play tennis?
-Of course.

164
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:15,440
Remember, according to your contract,
you can't play tennis.

165
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:17,640
I'll remind you,
that the day we'll make love

166
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:19,520
you'll cry for three days in a row.

167
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:21,240
-No doubt.
-We need to talk.

168
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:22,400
Later.

169
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:25,360
No, look who's here!

170
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:27,560
I forgot the best one of them all!

171
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:30,400
So how the hell are you?

172
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:32,480
Who the fuck are you?

173
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:35,760
I'm Alessandro, the new directing intern.

174
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:38,920
No. From now on you'll be...

175
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:41,440
Squid, right?

176
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:43,200
You'll be Squid. Do you like it?

177
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:46,560
And get used to it. I'm hilarious.
Squid! Keep it in mind.

178
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:54,440
RENÉ: Come on, Boris Becker.

179
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:57,040
Let's win the day. Want to?

180
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:58,880
How long for Corinna?

181
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:01,520
How long for Corinna?

182
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:02,920
MAN: Three minutes.

183
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:04,760
Okay. Now, you'll go over there.

184
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:10,840
And tell her that we'll start
with a very simple scene.

185
00:10:10,920 --> 00:10:13,440
But since she sucks,
she'll do it like crap.

186
00:10:13,520 --> 00:10:15,680
Go! (SNIFFS)

187
00:10:15,880 --> 00:10:18,200
Corinna. René sent me

188
00:10:18,280 --> 00:10:20,800
to say that we'll start
with a very difficult scene.

189
00:10:20,880 --> 00:10:22,600
He's sorry about that.

190
00:10:22,680 --> 00:10:25,960
But he says that,
since you're fantastic, you'll do great.

191
00:10:26,040 --> 00:10:27,040
Thank you.

192
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:30,280
RENÉ: I told you you'd become
a protagonist.

193
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:31,840
Didn't I tell you?

194
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:35,240
The called for a TV series.
You'd play a saint.

195
00:10:35,320 --> 00:10:36,640
A sort of female Padre Pio.

196
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:39,040
-Very nice.
-Isn't it too much makeup?

197
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:41,200
In this scene, she just woke up.

198
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:43,680
Don't listen to her.
Leave all the makeup on.

199
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:44,840
This is better.

200
00:10:46,560 --> 00:10:47,640
Did she leave?

201
00:10:48,200 --> 00:10:50,160
As I was saying, give it your all!

202
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:53,800
If things go according to plan,
you'll be the new Ferilli in two years.

203
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:56,680
(EXHALES SHARPLY)
Two years!

204
00:10:56,840 --> 00:10:58,200
(EXHALES SHARPLY)

205
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:01,680
Two years.

206
00:11:17,380 --> 00:11:18,380
Stanis?

207
00:11:19,300 --> 00:11:22,180
Do you remember the last scene
of The Eyes of the Heart 1?

208
00:11:23,220 --> 00:11:24,820
You're wearing the same thing.

209
00:11:24,900 --> 00:11:27,940
This coat and a stethoscope
around your neck, okay?

210
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:30,780
Stanis?

211
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:33,340
I'm so sorry.

212
00:11:33,420 --> 00:11:35,260
You're already in character, right?

213
00:11:35,940 --> 00:11:37,100
I'm sorry.

214
00:11:41,540 --> 00:11:44,060
-Hi, Stanis.
-God, we'll kick their ass. Come here.

215
00:11:44,220 --> 00:11:45,940
(KISSES)
This year, you and me...

216
00:11:46,020 --> 00:11:47,060
-Telegatti.
-Telegatti.

217
00:11:47,420 --> 00:11:50,100
(EXHALES SHARPLY)
Go!

218
00:11:50,180 --> 00:11:55,660
Okay, dear, let's film this right away.
We don't need to rehearse it.

219
00:11:55,740 --> 00:11:57,580
Stanis agrees.
Are you up for it?

220
00:11:57,660 --> 00:11:58,940
-Fine.
-Great!

221
00:11:59,020 --> 00:12:01,180
All right. Guys, let's go.

222
00:12:01,260 --> 00:12:03,620
We have another four pages
before the break.

223
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:07,220
Let's film, come on!
Let's change our mindset.

224
00:12:07,300 --> 00:12:09,260
This is scene is make or break for us.

225
00:12:09,340 --> 00:12:13,060
-Stanis, come on!
-We're rehearsing. God, you're so Italian!

226
00:12:13,540 --> 00:12:15,180
-My God!
-So annoying!

227
00:12:15,780 --> 00:12:17,060
When you're ready.

228
00:12:17,140 --> 00:12:18,700
I'm always perfect, right?

229
00:12:18,780 --> 00:12:19,940
Sorry, René.

230
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:22,460
Can we applaud for the first take?

231
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:28,660
All right, everyone.
An applause for Stanis and Corinna.

232
00:12:28,740 --> 00:12:29,980
And for the Maestro!

233
00:12:30,100 --> 00:12:32,540
-(ALL APPLAUDING)
-Well, thank you.

234
00:12:33,060 --> 00:12:34,300
Okay, let's roll.

235
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:38,540
The Eyes of the Heart 2, 168, first take.

236
00:12:40,020 --> 00:12:41,940
And action!

237
00:12:43,500 --> 00:12:46,620
Sometimes I'd like to...

238
00:12:47,620 --> 00:12:49,100
Start all over again.

239
00:12:49,180 --> 00:12:50,260
(WHISPERS)
She sucks.

240
00:12:50,340 --> 00:12:51,540
I don't know.

241
00:12:51,660 --> 00:12:54,900
Go someplace else,
where no one knows me.

242
00:12:55,020 --> 00:12:56,660
(WHISPERS)
Freaking ham!

243
00:12:57,300 --> 00:13:00,100
I don't know. Maybe change cities.

244
00:13:00,660 --> 00:13:03,140
I don't know. Challenge myself.

245
00:13:03,220 --> 00:13:04,820
I know this feeling.

246
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:06,220
(SIGHS)

247
00:13:06,340 --> 00:13:07,380
(EXHALES SHARPLY)

248
00:13:09,340 --> 00:13:10,380
It's called growing.

249
00:13:10,500 --> 00:13:11,620
(SIGHS)

250
00:13:12,020 --> 00:13:15,740
I'm 24 years old,
and they still think of me...

251
00:13:16,220 --> 00:13:17,660
-(WHISPERS)
-What the fuck is she saying?

252
00:13:17,740 --> 00:13:19,260
-34.
-Stop!

253
00:13:20,220 --> 00:13:23,020
It's 34. You have to say "34 years old."

254
00:13:23,100 --> 00:13:24,900
Sorry, but I'm not saying that.

255
00:13:24,980 --> 00:13:28,300
-What? Come on, again. 34.
-No. I won't say that.

256
00:13:28,380 --> 00:13:31,460
-You can't force me. How old do I look?
-RENÉ: Go talk to her.

257
00:13:31,540 --> 00:13:32,620
Corinna, I'm sorry...

258
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:36,700
-I refuse. I said no.
-What do you mean?

259
00:13:36,780 --> 00:13:39,300
Sorry, but how old are you? 31, 33?

260
00:13:39,380 --> 00:13:41,260
Everybody says I look 24, so I'm 24.

261
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:43,500
Sorry, Corinna, but there's a script.

262
00:13:43,580 --> 00:13:48,700
Scripts get changed. I talked to my agent,
to the network, and to Dr. Cane.

263
00:13:48,780 --> 00:13:51,380
He told me I can say anything I want.

264
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:58,260
CANE: Of course, sweetheart.
You can say anything you want.

265
00:13:58,900 --> 00:14:00,580
Just don't stop.

266
00:14:02,580 --> 00:14:03,620
Sergio!

267
00:14:04,340 --> 00:14:08,100
I don't know what to do. Solve this.
Call the network, whoever.

268
00:14:08,180 --> 00:14:12,540
-But I can't work in these conditions.
-Don't worry, I'll take care of it.

269
00:14:12,620 --> 00:14:15,580
Also, because, in five episodes,

270
00:14:15,660 --> 00:14:17,820
we find out that she has
a 13-year-old son!

271
00:14:17,900 --> 00:14:21,300
When did she have him? At 11?

272
00:14:21,380 --> 00:14:25,740
And last time I checked,
this series wasn't set in Cambodia!

273
00:14:25,820 --> 00:14:27,500
Biascica! Foosball.

274
00:14:27,620 --> 00:14:30,100
-Yes!
-I don't give a fuck!

275
00:14:30,180 --> 00:14:32,140
That bastard. How dare he?

276
00:14:32,260 --> 00:14:34,380
How old do you think
Anna Magnani was?

277
00:14:35,260 --> 00:14:36,820
How old do I look to you?

278
00:14:36,980 --> 00:14:40,420
Arnold was 80 and played a kid.
Like Shirley Temple.

279
00:14:40,540 --> 00:14:42,340
No!

280
00:14:42,500 --> 00:14:44,580
Come with me.
Can you play foosball?

281
00:14:44,660 --> 00:14:46,100
-I'm great at it.
-Brilliant.

282
00:14:46,180 --> 00:14:48,820
-Are you married or dating?
-My girlfriend's in Milan.

283
00:14:48,900 --> 00:14:50,220
-Come on!
-Don't get married.

284
00:14:50,300 --> 00:14:51,500
-No.
-What's your name?

285
00:14:51,580 --> 00:14:53,740
-Alessandro.
-Come, Fabrizio. You defend.

286
00:14:53,820 --> 00:14:56,620
There's scene 170
with the same set and clothes.

287
00:14:56,700 --> 00:14:59,100
I can have it ready in 15 minutes.
Right, Duccio?

288
00:14:59,180 --> 00:15:00,660
No, I'm busy now.

289
00:15:00,740 --> 00:15:04,820
I don't give a fuck. You know why?
It's not my problem. Nor yours.

290
00:15:04,900 --> 00:15:06,820
14-year-old boys have posters of me.

291
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:09,420
They don't care about my age.
(SIGHS)

292
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:11,340
Was the Gioconda really the Mona Lisa?

293
00:15:11,420 --> 00:15:14,340
No! It was Leonardo, a man!
Nobody tells the truth, come on!

294
00:15:14,420 --> 00:15:15,740
-Itala, please.
-What?

295
00:15:15,820 --> 00:15:17,820
Write on the daily production report:

296
00:15:17,900 --> 00:15:20,580
"Work suspended because of the network."
Come on!

297
00:15:20,660 --> 00:15:23,980
Go ask Duccio how much time he needs
to set up 170.

298
00:15:24,060 --> 00:15:27,740
I told you to drop it! I need him!
He needs to defend.

299
00:15:27,820 --> 00:15:29,860
And besides, I don't like the 170!

300
00:15:29,940 --> 00:15:32,900
Understood? I like the 168.
Come on, play!

301
00:15:32,980 --> 00:15:35,580
Dude. Duccio, 170.

302
00:15:35,740 --> 00:15:39,020
-Yes. It's Alessandro. Okay.
-Doesn't matter. Thanks. Go.

303
00:15:39,540 --> 00:15:40,660
RENÉ: Goal!

304
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:43,020
Goal.

305
00:15:47,380 --> 00:15:48,380
STUDIO 2

306
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:55,700
Duccio?

307
00:15:56,380 --> 00:15:57,620
(KNOCKING AT DOOR)

308
00:15:59,860 --> 00:16:01,540
(DOOR UNLOCKS)

309
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:09,300
(INHALES SHARPLY)

310
00:16:10,260 --> 00:16:14,020
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

311
00:16:14,900 --> 00:16:15,900
ALESSANDRO: Duccio?

312
00:16:18,380 --> 00:16:20,860
Listen, I'm thinking of quitting
the show.

313
00:16:22,020 --> 00:16:23,980
-Feel anything?
-Stop it, Stanis.

314
00:16:24,060 --> 00:16:25,740
No, I'm serious, Arianna.

315
00:16:26,020 --> 00:16:27,060
Because I'm unhappy.

316
00:16:27,140 --> 00:16:29,900
And when I'm unhappy,
my lawyers get moving.

317
00:16:29,980 --> 00:16:33,460
Do you know what they're doing?
They're getting me out of my contract.

318
00:16:33,580 --> 00:16:36,020
We already have problems.
Please, Stanis, behave.

319
00:16:36,100 --> 00:16:38,660
What do you think? Should I quit?

320
00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:40,700
Hey! Should I quit?

321
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:45,540
-You're a moron, Stanis.
-But Corinna sucks. She's too Italian.

322
00:16:46,620 --> 00:16:48,740
(SNIFFS) Sit down.

323
00:16:49,900 --> 00:16:52,260
(SIGHS) (SNIFFS)

324
00:16:54,260 --> 00:16:56,140
Did you watch the first two episodes?

325
00:16:57,860 --> 00:17:00,740
-Yes. Here and there.
-Did you like the cinematography?

326
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:02,500
(DUCCIO SNIFFS)

327
00:17:02,580 --> 00:17:03,580
Very much.

328
00:17:04,340 --> 00:17:05,660
You don't understand shit.

329
00:17:09,340 --> 00:17:11,260
The cinematography sucks.

330
00:17:12,140 --> 00:17:13,340
Do you know why?

331
00:17:14,340 --> 00:17:17,060
-I don't know.
-Because that's how they want it.

332
00:17:21,740 --> 00:17:22,940
It's what they want.

333
00:17:24,300 --> 00:17:28,220
The cinematography of a TV series
can't be better than the one in the ads,

334
00:17:28,300 --> 00:17:29,940
or people will change channels.

335
00:17:30,020 --> 00:17:31,580
They've thought of everything.

336
00:17:36,140 --> 00:17:37,180
Are you scared?

337
00:17:39,100 --> 00:17:43,460
-Arianna wants to know how long...
-Tell Arianna to fuck off.

338
00:17:44,900 --> 00:17:46,260
Fuck off.

339
00:17:48,980 --> 00:17:50,140
Fuck off.

340
00:17:51,020 --> 00:17:52,140
Fuck off!

341
00:17:52,580 --> 00:17:58,300
Hello? No. Someone made a big mistake,
my friend.

342
00:17:58,380 --> 00:18:01,660
-She has to say she's 34, nothing else.
-(EXHALES)

343
00:18:01,740 --> 00:18:03,420
No!

344
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:05,580
Hey, what did Duccio say?

345
00:18:05,700 --> 00:18:06,740
Ah...

346
00:18:07,180 --> 00:18:08,420
I couldn't find him.

347
00:18:08,500 --> 00:18:12,300
We'll solve it. Don't worry.

348
00:18:12,540 --> 00:18:14,780
Fine. No problem.

349
00:18:14,940 --> 00:18:18,540
Okay. Talk later. Goodbye.

350
00:18:19,180 --> 00:18:20,380
Bastards!

351
00:18:20,460 --> 00:18:24,660
They fuck things up
and then it's our fault! Right?

352
00:18:24,740 --> 00:18:26,140
What should we do?

353
00:18:26,380 --> 00:18:28,420
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

354
00:18:29,380 --> 00:18:31,940
(WHISPERS)
We'll film it.

355
00:18:34,420 --> 00:18:35,740
Dude. Come here.

356
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:38,580
-Here.
-What are we doing?

357
00:18:38,660 --> 00:18:41,460
Are we going home?
My daughter has a fever.

358
00:18:41,580 --> 00:18:43,460
We're taking care of the problem.

359
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:45,380
I was saying it for you.

360
00:18:46,380 --> 00:18:47,580
-Hi.
-Hi.

361
00:18:47,860 --> 00:18:49,740
I'm sorry about before.

362
00:18:50,340 --> 00:18:55,980
I also embarrassed myself
with Antonio Di Pollina from Repubblica.

363
00:18:56,180 --> 00:18:57,700
A journalist is here?

364
00:18:57,900 --> 00:19:01,140
Yes, that's him. He's terrible.

365
00:19:01,300 --> 00:19:04,740
We all belong to the left,
but then they always shit on TV.

366
00:19:04,820 --> 00:19:08,100
-Yeah.
-He's writing an article about us.

367
00:19:14,020 --> 00:19:15,860
-Hi.
-Hi.

368
00:19:16,540 --> 00:19:18,220
I'm sorry about before.

369
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:21,980
I don't know what happened.
I'm usually more relaxed.

370
00:19:22,060 --> 00:19:23,220
Ah, no worries.

371
00:19:24,420 --> 00:19:25,420
Are you Di Pollina?

372
00:19:25,980 --> 00:19:27,660
-What's your name?
-I'm Alessandro.

373
00:19:27,740 --> 00:19:30,540
STANIS: No, I'm gonna call you...
Do you like Squid?

374
00:19:30,620 --> 00:19:31,620
CORINNA:
Are you Di Pollina?

375
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:33,380
-If you want.
-Let's be informal.

376
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:35,020
Come, guys. Let's shoot.

377
00:19:35,100 --> 00:19:39,180
When I go home after work,
I always take a shower. Every day.

378
00:19:39,260 --> 00:19:41,580
I use a colored sponge.
Currently it's purple.

379
00:19:41,660 --> 00:19:43,380
And a scented body wash.

380
00:19:43,460 --> 00:19:45,900
It's raspberry, strawberry,
blueberry, and clementine.

381
00:19:46,460 --> 00:19:48,580
-Don't you write it down?
-What?

382
00:19:48,660 --> 00:19:50,500
Raspberry, strawberry, blueberry...

383
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:52,740
-I need to write it down?
-Of course!

384
00:19:52,820 --> 00:19:55,420
Come on, quick! Let's shoot.

385
00:19:55,500 --> 00:19:57,620
-What did you do?
-I'll tell you later.

386
00:19:57,700 --> 00:20:00,940
Send that dude home.
What's his name. The new intern.

387
00:20:01,020 --> 00:20:03,020
Kick him out. It's important.

388
00:20:03,100 --> 00:20:05,300
I'm posing for a calendar on Sunday.

389
00:20:05,380 --> 00:20:08,140
In the dunes of Capocotta,
with sand all over. Beautiful.

390
00:20:08,260 --> 00:20:10,700
-Come, if you want.
-Uh, this Sunday?

391
00:20:10,780 --> 00:20:13,180
-Yes. I'll give a photo.
-(SCOFFS)

392
00:20:13,340 --> 00:20:15,060
-First, I'll write...
-Okay.

393
00:20:15,140 --> 00:20:18,140
Maybe it's a provocation,
but I love TV series!

394
00:20:18,260 --> 00:20:22,140
My favorite album is Inno di Mameli,
a recent present.

395
00:20:22,220 --> 00:20:27,020
It makes me feel so emotional,
a part of a whole. Write. It's important.

396
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:29,660
-Let's reevaluate Italian music.
-Yes, I'm writing.

397
00:20:29,820 --> 00:20:31,460
Well, all right.

398
00:20:32,260 --> 00:20:34,300
Sorry, Corinna, we're ready to shoot.

399
00:20:34,420 --> 00:20:36,900
Okay. Let's exchange numbers later.

400
00:20:36,980 --> 00:20:38,460
-Yes.
-Remember, Sunday.

401
00:20:38,540 --> 00:20:40,180
-Okay.
-I'll gift you a photo.

402
00:20:42,020 --> 00:20:44,900
Well, what have you done
that now I have to kick you out?

403
00:20:45,860 --> 00:20:47,500
-Me?
-Out!

404
00:20:48,300 --> 00:20:49,300
-But...
-Out!

405
00:20:50,060 --> 00:20:51,060
But...

406
00:20:52,180 --> 00:20:53,180
Out.

407
00:20:58,140 --> 00:20:59,740
"Cherry and clementine?"

408
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:08,700
(MIMICKING SHOOTING)

409
00:21:08,780 --> 00:21:12,460
Come on! Let's go! Let's shoot.

410
00:21:13,020 --> 00:21:15,060
And rolling!

411
00:21:15,140 --> 00:21:17,220
Scene 168, second take.

412
00:21:18,220 --> 00:21:20,220
And action!

413
00:21:21,580 --> 00:21:24,940
Sometimes I'd like to...

414
00:21:25,700 --> 00:21:27,300
Start all over again.

415
00:21:27,380 --> 00:21:28,860
(WHISPERS)
Freaking ham.

416
00:21:28,940 --> 00:21:31,820
I don't know. Go someplace else,

417
00:21:31,900 --> 00:21:33,980
where no one knows me.

418
00:21:34,060 --> 00:21:36,780
I don't know. Maybe change cities.

419
00:21:37,300 --> 00:21:40,220
I don't know. Challenge myself.

420
00:21:40,300 --> 00:21:41,740
I know this feeling.

421
00:21:42,180 --> 00:21:43,340
(EXHALES)

422
00:21:43,660 --> 00:21:44,900
It's called growing.

423
00:21:45,140 --> 00:21:46,260
(EXHALES)

424
00:21:47,540 --> 00:21:48,540
I am...

425
00:21:48,860 --> 00:21:54,900
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

426
00:22:01,420 --> 00:22:02,460
The age that I am.

427
00:22:08,060 --> 00:22:09,140
And I really feel it.

428
00:22:10,700 --> 00:22:11,700
I really feel it.

429
00:22:11,860 --> 00:22:13,260
(SIGHS WEARILY)

430
00:22:13,580 --> 00:22:14,900
Stop! Great!

431
00:22:16,220 --> 00:22:18,580
STUDIO 3

432
00:22:19,660 --> 00:22:21,820
They kicked me out. Yes.

433
00:22:22,940 --> 00:22:24,980
No. I didn't do anything.

434
00:22:26,740 --> 00:22:28,340
I don't know why.

435
00:22:29,500 --> 00:22:32,540
-Hey, dude.
-Just a minute.

436
00:22:32,620 --> 00:22:34,900
Tomorrow, 7:30 A.M. On time.

437
00:22:37,020 --> 00:22:38,860
Watch it. You're already on notice.

438
00:22:40,100 --> 00:22:42,700
Hello? No, I'm coming back tomorrow.

439
00:22:42,860 --> 00:22:46,900
I know I just told you.
But here things change quickly.

440
00:22:46,980 --> 00:22:50,540
I'll call you from home. Okay.
Yes, I'll tell you everything. Bye.

441
00:22:54,420 --> 00:22:57,100
(THEME SONG PLAYING)
